# The harmonics (power-of-N) module's bottom toolbar (SA_UI_SPEC.md section 5).
# Control is SA's caption: keep it; translate the hints.

hm-control = Control
    .hover = Draw a marker line at the carrier: align the spectral line with it to read the exact carrier
hm-carrier-down = Carrier down 1 Hz
hm-carrier-down-fast = Carrier down 10 Hz
hm-carrier-up-fast = Carrier up 10 Hz
hm-carrier-up = Carrier up 1 Hz
hm-carrier = Carrier frequency, Hz: the Control line is drawn at it
    .hover = Carrier frequency, Hz: the Control line is drawn at it
hm-compute = Compute with the current settings
hm-busy = Wait until the work in progress ends
hm-power-down = Lower harmonic
hm-power-up = Higher harmonic
hm-power = Harmonic (power) of the signal studied, 2-32
    .hover = Harmonic (power) of the signal studied, 2-32
hm-carrier-invalid = Carrier is not a number; enter it in whole Hz, such as 1800.
